Forecasting an outbreak works by taking a running count of infections and separating two questions

00:07:34.862 --> 00:07:39.442
that traders often mash together, when the wave crests and how large it gets.

00:07:40.142 --> 00:07:44.482
The papers in front of me fit a model to past weeks and then fold in new observations,

00:07:45.042 --> 00:07:49.822
the same habit as a weather model swallowing a fresh reading. None of them is an exchange.

00:07:49.822 --> 00:07:55.262
range. None of the abstracts names a contract, a traitor, or a payout. The New York City

00:07:55.262 --> 00:07:59.902
study in the proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences is the example with a clock on

00:07:59.902 --> 00:08:06.022
it. For the seasons from 2003 through 2008, researchers took weekly web estimates of

00:08:06.022 --> 00:08:10.962
local infection rates, assimilated them, and after each update built a retrospective

00:08:10.962 --> 00:08:16.642
ensemble. Many runs, not one line. They found real-time skill on the timing of the peak

00:08:16.642 --> 00:08:21.742
more than seven weeks before the peak actually arrived. The confidence measure was the spread of

00:08:21.742 --> 00:08:27.342
those runs. When the bundle was tight, the timing calls agreed. When it was wide, they did not.

00:08:28.022 --> 00:08:34.242
Melbourne splits timing from size. A bootstrap particle filter and a mechanistic infection model fed

00:08:34.242 --> 00:08:40.782
with Google Flu trends from 2006 through 2014 called the peak accurately four to six weeks ahead.

00:08:41.302 --> 00:08:45.622
How high that peak would be and how heavy the whole season would be were much harder.

00:08:45.622 --> 00:08:50.562
The team picked among hundreds of observation models by scoring forecasts the way someone

00:08:50.562 --> 00:08:53.202
reads a receiver operating characteristic curve.

00:08:53.522 --> 00:09:00.242
In Fujo, four regressions, Sarima, Prophet, Holt Winters, and XG Boost were fit on cases

00:09:00.242 --> 00:09:05.462
from January 2013 through December 2021 and scored on 2022.

00:09:06.242 --> 00:09:11.442
XG Boost posted the lowest mean-squared error, the lowest root mean-squared error, and the

00:09:11.442 --> 00:09:15.182
the lowest mean absolute error on both the training set and the test set.

00:09:15.322 --> 00:09:19.562
That series was seasonal, cyclical, trending up, and jumpy.

